🐛 Describe the bug
When building PyTorch with clang++-17 -std=gnu++20 -x c++, the macro  


      pytorch/c10/util/bit_cast.h


         Line 6
      in
      d23051f







           #if __has_include(<bit>) && (__cplusplus >= 202002L || (defined(__cpp_lib_bit_cast) && __cpp_lib_bit_cast >= 201806L)) 




 decides to use bit_cast from standard C++ library. However, that version of clang++-17 does NOT implement it, so a link error happens. To fix this macro, I propose to change the condition
#if __has_include(<bit>) && (__cplusplus >= 202002L || (defined(__cpp_lib_bit_cast) && __cpp_lib_bit_cast >= 201806L))
to
#if __has_include(<bit>) && defined(__cpp_lib_bit_cast) && __cpp_lib_bit_cast >= 201806L
FYI: clang++-17 version
Ubuntu clang version 17.0.6 (++20231208085846+6009708b4367-1exp120231208085949.74)
